!.env.example
*.keystore
*.jks
google-services.json
local.properties
# Private key material and certificate containers. specs/015 research.md R30
# claimed these were added; they were not, which is why the only thing standing
# between a committed signing key and `git add -A` used to be the `.env` lines
# above. Verified against `git ls-files` first: the only key/cert files tracked
# today are quiche's upstream example fixtures, listed as explicit negations
# below so a re-vendor cannot accidentally drop them and so nobody reads these
# patterns as an oversight.
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.crt
# !  Upstream vendored example certificates/keys (test fixtures, not secrets):
!quiche/apps/src/bin/cert.key
!quiche/apps/src/bin/cert.crt
!quiche/fuzz/cert.key
!quiche/fuzz/cert.crt
!quiche/quiche/examples/cert.key
!quiche/quiche/examples/cert.crt
!quiche/quiche/examples/cert-big.crt
!quiche/quiche/examples/rootca.crt
!quiche/tokio-quiche/examples/cert.key
!quiche/tokio-quiche/examples/cert.crt

# ── Archives (do not commit build products) ───────────────────
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
# There used to be a `!packaging/**` here. A blanket un-ignore of an entire
# subtree sitting directly beside the code that mints installers means a committed
# `packaging/windows-x64.zip` would have bypassed this rule with no review signal.
# Nothing under packaging/ is an archive today (`git ls-files packaging` = 3 text
# files + wintun.dll), so the exception is gone. Re-add it BY FILE NAME, in the
# commit that adds the asset, never by subtree.

# ⚙ Runtime Configs & State
# Anchored to the repository root and no longer a bare `aether*` prefix: the
# unanchored form matched ANY directory in the tree, so a legitimate future asset
# - apps/desktop/src-tauri/aether.config.json, Docs/aether-notes.toml - would be
# silently un-addable, which is the same class of bug as the archive exception
# above. Local scratch files produced by the tooling live at the root.
/aether*.toml
/aether*.json

# ── Qoder / AI tooling artifacts ─────────────────────────────
.qoder/
.agents/
.opencode/
.specify/
# Keep specs visible to codebase-memory indexing.
PRODUCT.md
architecture-review-*.html
test_engine.log
